Neo4j. The data model is:
```
(s\:Site)-\[:HAS\_FEATURE]->(f\:Feature)
(f\:Feature)-\[:HAS\_ROCKART]->(m\:RockArtMotif)
(a\:Site)-\[:CLOSE\_TO\_SITE {distance\_m}]-(b\:Site)
(a\:Feature)-\[:CLOSE\_TO\_FEATURE {distance\_m}]-(b\:Feature)
(f\:Feature)-\[:NEAR {distance\_m}]-(s\:Site)
```
Each node has a `location` property (Neo4j point, WGS-84) derived from `Lat`/`Lon`.
Use `point.distance(a.location, b.location)` for arbitrary distance calculations.
Use `CLOSE_TO_SITE` / `CLOSE_TO_FEATURE` relationships (pre-computed, < 500 m) for same-type proximity.
Use `NEAR` relationships (pre-computed, < 500 m) for cross-type proximity (Feature near a non-parent Site).
IMPORTANT: `CLOSE_TO_*` and `NEAR` relationships are stored unidirectionally. Always use **undirected** patterns (`-[:CLOSE_TO_SITE]-` without `>`) to find all neighbors.
